---
const toolset = [
  { group: 'Every day', items: ['React', 'TypeScript', 'CSS', 'HTML', 'Design systems', 'Accessibility (WCAG)', 'Performance'] },
  { group: 'Also shipped with', items: ['Astro', 'Svelte 5', 'Vite', 'Radix UI', 'Tailwind', 'Motion', 'SVG data visualization'] },
  { group: 'Testing', items: ['Jest', 'Testing Library', 'Playwright', 'Cypress', 'axe-core'] },
  { group: 'Server side', items: ['Node', 'WebSockets', 'Python and FastAPI', 'React on Ruby on Rails backends'] },
  { group: 'AI in the loop', items: ['Claude Code', 'Codex', 'Cursor', 'Agent skills and review pipelines', 'Streaming LLM output'] },
];
---

<section id="about" class="about surface" data-paint aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <h2 id="about-title" class="t-section">How I got here</h2>
      <div class="about-copy prose">
        <p class="t-lede">
          I found Scratch at 8 or 9 and fell in love with it. Before high school I ran a website of flash games packaged for
          the offline laptops kids used at school, and it got more than 300,000 page views from other children. I was hooked on
          making ideas real, and later made the national top ten of ANIMATE, Uruguay’s animation contest, two years in a row.
        </p>
        <p>
          I still care most about the same thing: interfaces people can trust. Complex UIs and performance work are what I enjoy
          most, especially main thread management and keeping things responsive under heavy data.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’ve used LLMs for my work since GPT-3, and today agents are part of how I build. At Cisco that meant building the
          guardrails before scaling the output. In my own products it means I own the product thinking, design direction,
          architecture and review, and every one of them started from a written brief and a design spec, with the bigger ones
          recording their decisions as ADRs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="toolset">
      {
        toolset.map((t) => (
          <div class="toolset-row">
            <dt class="t-label">{t.group}</dt>
            <dd>{t.items.join(', ')}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: var(--section-y); }
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 32px clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .about-copy { font-size: 1.125rem; }
  .about-copy p:not(.t-lede) { color: var(--s-muted); }
  .about-copy .t-lede { color: var(--s-ink); }

  .toolset {
    margin: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--s-ink);
  }
  .toolset-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: 8px clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    padding-block: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--s-rule);
  }
  .toolset-row dt { padding-top: 3px; }
  .toolset-row dd { font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 520; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-grid,
    .toolset-row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
